    Install markdownlint if needed (#7669)
    
    This PR checks to see if markdownlint is installed (globally, and
    locally), and if not then uses npm to install it.
    
    This facilitates testing locally since some of us (me) don't have
    markdownlint installed.
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    Ensure markdownlint isn't installed, then run
    `./docs/checkstyle/check-docs.sh`. If markdownlint is missing you will
    see a failure without this patch. With it you will see a line about
    installing markdownlint. If you have it installed already, or on
    subsequent runs without a `git clean` you won't see a lint at all.
    
    Targetting legacy since I'm still working in it and see test failures
    regularly.
    
